d-3766dfdd452a4fed","cmd-76ba272ea4fa4fb3","cmd-cd6648bf09d64dc4","cmd-f413e2abc02746dc","cmd-da3210027c2d4c38","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol was performed on both nodes: healthy pre-restart states and acknowledgements were captured, boot identities changed and match the fixed lifecycle observations, configurations persisted, and final cluster synchronization recovered.","limitations":["Recovery after each restart was not fully autonomous within the captured waiting periods: node1 and node2 required bounded one-shot ntpd -gq corrective actions before final leap=00/kernel-synchronized states were obtained. Restart persistence is not an explicit public-task requirement, but this weakens evidence of unattended recovery.","The fixed after-executor listening-socket snapshots are empty despite direct executor commands showing node1 listening on UDP/123; the direct commands and node2's successful synchronization support functionality, but the supplemental snapshot is not independently corroborative.","The bounded lifecycle inventory does not inspect retained /etc configuration-backup files, so their final presence cannot be independently determined."]}
